This build context embeds Ubisoft La Forge's CHORD inference code
(https://github.com/ubisoft/ubisoft-laforge-chord, Ubisoft Machine Learning License
(Research-Only - Copyleft)) at commit 675a29d1fee5e1b256833bd4edabd619be43d0c7.
The vendored archive is a deterministic subset of that commit: LICENSE,
config/chord.yaml and the chord/ package, every member byte-identical to the
upstream file at that commit (sorted members, mtime 0). The creator's test.py and
demo_gradio.py, its examples and assets, and its requirements.txt are left out:
pipelines/infer.py repeats test.py's inference steps against the vendored package,
and the dependencies are locked in requirements.lock. The Docker build verifies the
archive SHA-256 before extraction. The vendored LICENSE applies to this code and to
the model weights, which are not part of this build context.

Nothing is patched. The creator's StableDiffusion module already loads its UNet, VAE,
text-encoder configuration and tokenizer from a local directory when the config names
one (hf_key); pipelines/infer.py sets that key to the read-only /models mount and
loads chord_v1.safetensors from /models, so no file is fetched at run time.

The files under pipelines/ are Vonk Forge wrappers for the signed job contract.
